  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SECURING HABITAT FOR SUSTAINABLE FUTURE OF RHINO TIGER IN CHITWAN PARSA COMPLEX, NEPAL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds under this award are to be used to ensure the survival of the dispersing tigers from Chitwan and Bardia National Parks and maintain the genetic linkages between them. Project objectives are to, (1) upgrade habitat in Chitwan Parsa Complex, (2) improve status of grassland and wetland dwelling wild animals, and, (3) build national capacity on habitat management. Chitwan National Park, Parsa National Park, conservation organizations, local communities, rhinos (&gt;600 individuals) and tigers (~110 individuals), and other wild animals of Chitwan-Parsa Complex will benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
